{
 "id": "client-compaction/ends-replay-then-new-change/hot/5m",
 "description": "One cmdfilter change is reported on request 1 and applied again on request 2 (+$0.02625 as new content, +$0.00210 as a read). On request 3 the client compacts: a summary replaces message 0, so the provider reads only the system block and the client body would have done the same. The change has ended (design \u00a74.3): it has no operation on request 3 or later, and nothing is replayed across the compaction. The break has an empty ChangeID and moves no tokens, because B* is the system block. On request 5 the same operator shortens a new output: a new change, priced in full as a write.",
 "source": "issue_cases.md",
